("BSD").
We checked the given link and found in the repo the BSD-3-Clause license, which we took for conclusion and the text of the GPL-2.0-only. The README file states:"This repository represents the reference implementation, provided as an open-source dual BSD and GPLv2 licensed C library, and a command line utility producing and decoding"
Thus we concluded GPL-2.0-only or BSD-3-Clause as license of this file.
We could not find any patent license grant in the repo
The information was retrieved on 15th of July 2023 </text>
